settings_connection#:#Tarsus connection
settings_connection_desc#:#Connect this installation to Tarsus. One brain per installation. Tarsus activates API keys and brain IDs by hand. There are no private test brains: for testing, Tarsus provides one sandbox brain shared by all partners, and every request on it is billed like any other – the plugin's own mock mode (below) is the only free way to try things.
apikey#:#API key
apikey_desc#:#The Tarsus API key. Stored in the database and never sent to the browser.
apikey_keep#:#A key is stored; leave the field empty to keep it.
apikey_none#:#No key is stored yet.
brainid#:#Brain ID
brainid_desc#:#The single Tarsus brain used by this installation (partner customers). Not sent while a license key is stored. Pick one of the brains the API key can reach:
brainid_sandbox#:#For testing, use the sandbox brain Tarsus provides to all partners – its requests are billed too.
brain_sandbox_note#:#Tarsus activates brains by hand. There are no private test brains: for testing, use the sandbox brain Tarsus provides to all partners – every request on it is billed like any other. The plugin's mock mode (Settings) is the only free way to try things.
licensekey#:#License key
licensekey_desc#:#Only for existing Tarsus customers: they carry a license key in addition to the API key and in place of a brain ID. While one is stored, every call sends the API key and the license key – and no brain ID – and Tarsus, not the partner, bills the usage. Stored in the database and never sent to the browser.
licensekey_keep#:#A license key is stored; leave the field empty to keep it.
licensekey_none#:#No license key is stored (partner customer).
licensekey_clear#:#Remove the license key
licensekey_clear_desc#:#The customer becomes a partner customer again: billed by the partner, calls carry the brain ID.
baseurl#:#Base URL
baseurl_desc#:#The Tarsus API base URL. Enter only the host, e.g. https://api.example.org, without the /api/v1/... path.
error_baseurl#:#Enter a URL starting with http:// or https://.
settings_assistant#:#Assistant
settings_assistant_desc#:#How the AI assistant introduces itself in the chat. One identity for the whole installation.
robotname#:#Assistant name
robotname_desc#:#The name of the AI assistant, as learners see it.
robotid#:#Assistant ID
robotid_desc#:#The id of this assistant on the Tarsus side, as provided by Tarsus. Defaults to the name.
